{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Publish a national food emergency plan and assess strategic food reserves",
        "additional_details": "The UK food system relies on domestic production and complex international supply chains that can be disrupted by extreme weather, conflict, trade or energy shortages and other emergencies.\r\n\r\nWe want the Government to assess how essential food supplies would be maintained during a prolonged disruption, identify critical vulnerabilities, consider whether strategic reserves of staple foods would improve resilience, and explain how essential food would be distributed fairly, particularly to vulnerable people.\r\n\r\nThis is about preparedness, not predicting shortages.",
        "background": "We want the Government to establish and publish a national food emergency plan for major or prolonged disruption to UK food supplies, and to assess the case for maintaining strategic reserves of essential foods.",
